# Receipts: what a gate proved, bound to the content it proved it on
# (scripts/gates/receipts.py). commit-gate.json is the tree the pre-commit hook
# checks; assurance-gate.json binds the e2e behaviour verdicts to HEAD's tree;
# publish-gate.json binds the publish gate to exact local image IDs; and
# image-candidates/<rev>.json records the digest set a candidate was validated
# with, which edge promotion consumes. They describe one clone's validation
# state, so they are never committed — but this directory is, so a fresh clone
# has somewhere to put them and this rule is in force before the first receipt.
#
# The rule is load-bearing, not tidiness. A receipt names a tree hash; a
# *tracked* receipt would be part of the tree it measures, so writing one would
# change the answer and no receipt could ever match twice. receipts.write refuses
# a receipt git does not ignore, so if this rule is ever edited away the gate
# fails loudly instead of silently rejecting every commit.
*
!.gitignore
